# Home Assistant official container uses s6-overlay which requires root at startup to initialize runtime daemons (s6-svscan, s6-sudod, go2rtc)
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118 (Default security context configured)
KSV-0118
AVD-KSV-0118

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# Home Assistant s6-overlay entrypoint requires default capabilities for s6 process management and hardware/device access
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106

# Home Assistant configuration.yaml uses '!secret' references; sensitive values are mounted via Kubernetes Secret at /config/secrets.yaml
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0109 (ConfigMap with secrets)
KSV-0109
AVD-KSV-0109
